## GRADING (binding; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (D1).** A second path or a product byte = **Blocker** (STOP: hand-up if security-shaped); a removed or changed existing line = **Major, class (d)**; a person's name, secret or card slug = **Blocker**; non-ASCII or a skip/only/timer = **Major**; `localdomain` = **Major**; a false commit sentence = **Minor** (corrected in `squash-body.txt`); a Jira key or work number in an added line = **Minor**.
- **G-2 the claim (D3, D5).** The named edit `(\D\d{3})` NOT failing the file at setup, or any row running under it = **Major, class (a)**; a title clause a run does not back = **Major, class (e)** if it is the kill claim, **Minor** otherwise; the title over- or under-claiming which year-class edits it covers (k2) = **Minor** (fix-shape in prose); the first `expect` decorative (unreachable whenever the setup passes, p4) = **Note** when the second `expect` carries the row, **Minor** if nothing else can fail.
- **G-3 the row (D2, D3, D4).** The row green under every plant of yours that breaks what it asserts = **Major, class (b)**; red or flaky unplanted (any of the 3 runs, the shuffle) = **Major, class (c)**; a plant that reddens rows the builder did not report = **Minor** (a number) unless it hides a defect; lint or prettier rc non-zero on the file = **Major** (CI's node step fails); the duplicate import allowed by the config and lint rc 0 = **Note** (style); the group other than main + 0 files + 1 test, or names other than lost 0 / added 1 = **Major** unless explained; no tsc covering `apps/api/test` = **Note** (not this lane).
- **G-4 merge and CodeQL (D6).** A conflict with main or Part A, or a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; an open alert = **Blocker** and STOP; CodeQL NOT SCANNED (no PR) = a **Condition**. **Always Note:** the builder's container overrun, the dependabot banner.
- **G-5 verdict (round 1 of 2).** Any Blocker or Major = `NO GO (round 1 of 2)` (fix-shapes in prose; "a second NO GO on this class goes to the product owner on a card"); Minors/Notes only = `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`; none above Note = `GO`. Always add ` (conditional: NO PR; CodeQL NOT SCANNED)` and any other unrun required check.

## LOAD (binding)
8 cores shared (load1 2.48 at 11:10; HPSM-POC-R109 and -D43 live; B1037 may be running). Heavy = `docker build`, any container run, any vitest run. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent: say so), recorded beside each result. **One heavy job at a time, behind your seat lock `.tools/b1038/lock` AND the project lock `.tools/composer-heavy.lock`; you WAIT on B1037's holder.** A MOVING heartbeat to `.tools/b1038/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a wait loop never uses `pgrep -f`/`ps | grep` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets `/dev/null` or its input. Budget (write it at Step 0, about 16 starts, each `dbtest.sh` run = 2: postgres + node): build 1, main file 2, head x3 6, row alone and shuffle 2-4 (batch), plants k1 (head and main test), p1-p4 about 10 (batch several into one container pair where your harness allows: say how), group head and main 4. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b1038-*` containers, networks and anonymous volumes, by exact name.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh, no HTTP to any hosted host or the demo site. Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` a container you did not create. Network: your one in-clone fetch, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`; no POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE, no `gh pr create`, no re-run. Git in `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`), worktree add ONLY `.tools/wt-b1038-{main,head,mut}` detached (assert `HEAD` and `HEAD^{tree}`); clone/fetch/merge-tree only in `.tools/b1038/repo`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` or `inbound/`. No decision-queue, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` beyond the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (quarantine to `.tools/b1038/quarantine/`; do not type `rm`). **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (space and `!`); `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script (zsh is the interactive shell); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I -B`; write programs with the Write tool and read them back. Plants live ONLY in `wt-b1038-mut`. Synthetic data only. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"), no card slug. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR WORK section in STATUS (what you read of the builder lane; what you reuse: plumbing only); Jira writes none; nothing to any human. **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections, plants restored with proof, processes and containers stopped, both locks released by move, last line `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?`.

